    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d213">

                <pb facs="0321" n="301" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/7–350: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Muccio</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Taejon</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1950-07-03T23:00:00+10:00">July 3, 1950—11 p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 4—4:14 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>10. Mytel 7, July 3.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d213-f1"/> Enemy thrusts through Yongen
                    and Songjongni do not appear to have made much progress today. Enemy believed to
                    have pushed considerable number troops and equipment across Han River below
                    Seoul with air opposition seemingly light. New threat has developed to east,
                    this time in Yoju and Wonju areas which reportedly in enemy hands and with enemy
                    advancing rapidly southeast. This enemy thrust evidently came from Chunchon
                    direction and represents break through 6th division defenses.</p>
                <p>Rhee arrived in Pusan yesterday by sea from Mokpo and is evincing strong desire
                    return Taejon. About 105 assemblymen have registered with Assembly secretariat
                    and others are known to have gone <pb facs="0322" n="302" xml:id="pg302"/> to
                    constituencies in south. Cabinet had inaugurated informal meetings, though there
                    little evidence of government offices being set up in Taejon. People more calm
                    here today than any time since outbreak hostilities. Commodity prices have risen
                    somewhat Taejon where influx of refugees relatively great, but little
                    elsewhere.</p>
                <p>Department pass CINCFE.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Muccio</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
